MXL\/MXLStaffDetails","title":"MXLStaffDetails","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLStaffDetails","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The staff-details element is used to indicate different types of staves. The optional number attribute","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specifies the staff number from top to bottom on the system, as with clef. The print-object attribute is used","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to indicate when a staff is not printed in a part, usually in large scores where empty parts are omitted. It","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is yes by default. If print-spacing is yes while print-object is no, the score is printed in cutaway format","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"where vertical space is left for the empty part.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffdetails"}}}